  "behavior": [
    "Actual Pooling table and selected layout move into fresh state without inheriting old inference retention. Native copies preserve independent primary/index streams and original logical partial windows.",
    "The shared source-bound saved-resume driver, atomic source validation, prompt completion, sampling preparation, target exchange and opening readiness remain the sole execution route.",
    "A sealed registered isolated-copy program composes full source-inclusive diagnostics and a reduced reservation. Existing native decoder/key sources receive one physical-source credit, while each copied destination stays priced.",
    "Complete saved source origins, credited origins and source account health validate under the reservation lock. Old charges never refund, and pins survive until native completion or quarantine.",
    "Core resolves admitted floating capture selection geometry without allocation. Runtime alone allocates exact fixed shape/data capacities under a closed private host-only account; whole construction hold remains through last alias.",
    "Incomplete capture construction retains its buffers and custody. Read-only shared aliases and borrowed capture wire serialization avoid implicit payload copies."
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "After these checks passed, independent review of the next no-decoder constructor found a shared funding quarantine first-inventory assumption. That concrete gap is retained explicitly as a limitation pending the next focused fix.",
    "Root reviewed original packages and rebase deltas. Grouped exports, child-table publication and full source inventory remain intact; incremental export and HostOnly coexist with grouped funding.",
    "Independent neutral/native source-credit reviews found no concrete blocker; complete source pinning remains broader than credited copy operands.",
